1.PMBRS is a personal behavioral measurement, experimentation, and representation learning platform designed to discover reproducible statistical associations between behaviors, interventions, contexts, and outcomes using multimodal longitudinal data. Its purpose is to support structured self-experimentation, behavioral comparison, and evidence-informed personal interpretation rather than deterministic inference, diagnosis, or automated behavioral prescription.

2.
PMBRS is explicitly out of scope for clinical diagnosis, deterministic mental-state inference, automatic causal claims, simplistic productivity scoring, automated behavioral prescriptions, commercial product concerns, real-time intervention systems, and exhaustive raw surveillance. Its purpose is limited to discovering statistically supported behavioral associations for personal experimentation and interpretation. PMBRS does not autonomously optimize, manipulate, or intervene in user behavior through closed-loop behavioral control systems.


